IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpfta-types`
IMPORT `cpfta-part1`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Part 2 (ss 3 to 5) and the
-- Second Schedule.  Source: source/CPFTA2003.txt lines 254 to 309 and 2403 to 2567.
-- The remedies and procedure of Part 2 (ss 6 to 12) are in cpfta-part2-redress.l4.

§ `Part 2 -- Unfair practices`

§§ `3. Application of Part`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 3(a) and (b)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Application Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 applies` IF
        a's `the supplier is resident in Singapore`
     OR a's `the consumer is resident in Singapore`
     OR a's `the offer relating to the consumer transaction is made in Singapore`
     OR a's `the offer relating to the consumer transaction is sent from Singapore`
     OR a's `the acceptance relating to the consumer transaction is made in Singapore`
     OR a's `the acceptance relating to the consumer transaction is sent from Singapore`

§§ `4. Meaning of unfair practice`

-- The opening words: "for a supplier, in relation to a consumer transaction".
-- 4(d) "without limiting paragraphs (a), (b) and (c)": the Second Schedule adds
-- to, and does not narrow, the general limbs.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 4(a)"
GIVEN u IS AN `Unfair Practice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(a) is satisfied` IF
        u's `the supplier does or says something, or omits to do or say something`
    AND u's `as a result a consumer might reasonably be deceived or misled`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 4(b)"
GIVEN u IS AN `Unfair Practice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(b) is satisfied` IF
    u's `the supplier makes a false claim`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 4(c)(i) and (ii)"
GIVEN u IS AN `Unfair Practice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(c) is satisfied` IF
        u's `the supplier takes advantage of a consumer`
    AND (   u's `the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the consumer is not in a position to protect his or her own interests`
         OR u's `the supplier knows or ought reasonably to know that the consumer is not reasonably able to understand the character, nature, language or effect of the transaction or any matter related to the transaction`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 4(d) and Second Schedule, Part 1"
GIVEN u IS AN `Unfair Practice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4(d) is satisfied` IF
    any (GIVEN p YIELD `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` p)
        (u's `the practices specified in the Second Schedule that the supplier engages in`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 4"
GIVEN u IS AN `Unfair Practice Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier engages in an unfair practice` IF
        u's `the supplier acts in relation to a consumer transaction`
    AND (   `section 4(a) is satisfied` u
         OR `section 4(b) is satisfied` u
         OR `section 4(c) is satisfied` u
         OR `section 4(d) is satisfied` u)

§§ `5. Circumstances surrounding unfair practice`

-- 5(1) "An unfair practice may occur before, during or after a consumer
-- transaction" and 5(2) "may consist of a single act or omission" widen what
-- can count; they impose no test of their own.  They are why `the supplier
-- engages in an unfair practice` takes no facts about timing or repetition.
-- 5(3)(a), that the reasonableness of the person's actions is considered,
-- directs the fact-finder and is the reason s 4(a) and (c) turn on what is
-- reasonable, not on what the supplier intended.  All three are inert.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, s 5(3)(b)(i) and (ii)"
GIVEN a IS AN `Attribution Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act or omission of an employee or agent is also that of the person` IF
        (    a's `the act or omission is that of an employee`
         AND a's `the employee acted in the course of the employee's employment with the person`)
     OR (    a's `the act or omission is that of an agent`
         AND a's `the agent was exercising powers or performing duties on behalf of the person`
         AND a's `the agent acted within the scope of the agent's actual or apparent authority`)

§§ `Second Schedule, Part 2 -- Interpretation`

-- Paragraph 2 says that a request, an intention to accept and pay, or a consent
-- is "not to be inferred only from" payment, use, dealing or disposal, a request
-- to purchase another similar good or service, or inaction.  The facts record a
-- finding that a request or consent exists and, separately, whether the only
-- ground for it is one of those four; a finding resting only on those grounds
-- does not count.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraph 1(a) and paragraph 2"
GIVEN f IS AN `Unsolicited Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods or services were requested by the consumer` IF
        f's `the consumer requested the goods or services`
    AND NOT f's `the only ground for finding a request is one of payment, use, dealing or disposal, a request to purchase another similar good or service, or inaction`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraph 1(b) and paragraph 2"
GIVEN f IS AN `Unsolicited Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumer consented to the material change` IF
        f's `the consumer consented in writing to the material change`
    AND NOT f's `the only ground for finding consent to the material change is payment, use, dealing or disposal, a request to purchase another similar good or service, or inaction`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraph 1(a)"
GIVEN f IS AN `Unsolicited Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods or services are unsolicited under paragraph 1(a)` IF
        f's `the goods or services are supplied in relation to a consumer transaction to a consumer`
    AND NOT `the goods or services were requested by the consumer` f
    AND NOT (    f's `the consumer knows or ought to have known that the goods or services were intended for delivery to another person`
             AND NOT f's `it was reasonable to believe that the goods or services, if delivered to that other person, would have been unsolicited`)

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraph 1(b)"
GIVEN f IS AN `Unsolicited Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods or services are unsolicited under paragraph 1(b)` IF
        f's `the goods or services are supplied on a continuing basis`
    AND f's `there is a material change in the goods or services, or in their supply`
    AND NOT `the consumer consented to the material change` f

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraph 1"
GIVEN f IS AN `Unsolicited Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the goods or services are unsolicited goods or services` IF
        `the goods or services are unsolicited under paragraph 1(a)` f
     OR `the goods or services are unsolicited under paragraph 1(b)` f

-- Paragraph 3(2): "any deposit paid by the consumer ... is treated as an instalment".

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 2, paragraph 3(1) and (2)"
GIVEN g IS AN `Applicable Agreement Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is an applicable agreement` IF
        g's `the agreement is between a supplier and a consumer for the supply of goods or services`
    AND g's `the agreement expressly provides that the goods or services will not be supplied, or begin to be supplied, until the price or part of the price has been paid`
    AND g's `the agreement expressly provides that the price is to be paid by instalments`
    AND (   g's `the number of instalments, not counting any deposit`
          PLUS (IF g's `the consumer has paid a deposit` THEN 1 ELSE 0))
        AT LEAST 2

§§ `Second Schedule, Part 1 -- Specific unfair practices`

-- A representation "if [it is] not [so]" is a made representation whose content is
-- not in fact accurate.

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 1, paragraphs 1, 2, 4, 8, 9, 12, 18 and 21"
GIVEN r IS A Representation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the representation is made and is untrue` IF
        r's `the representation is made`
    AND NOT r's `the representation is accurate`

@ref "Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, Second Schedule, Part 1, paragraphs 1 to 27"
GIVEN p IS A `Second Schedule Practice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the practice is specified in the Second Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER p
    -- 1. Representing that goods or services have sponsorship, approval, performance
    --    characteristics, accessories, ingredients, components, qualities, uses or
    --    benefits that they do not have.
    WHEN `Paragraph 1` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 2. Representing that the supplier has a sponsorship, approval or affiliation
    --    that the supplier does not have.
    WHEN `Paragraph 2` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 3. Making a false or misleading representation concerning the need for any
    --    goods or services.
    WHEN `Paragraph 3` r fm THEN
            r's `the representation is made` AND fm
    -- 4. Representing that goods or services are of a particular standard, quality,
    --    grade, style, model, origin, weight, volume, length, capacity or method of
    --    manufacture if they are not.
    WHEN `Paragraph 4` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 5. Representing that goods are new or unused if they are not or if they have
    --    deteriorated or been altered, reconditioned or reclaimed.
    WHEN `Paragraph 5` r det THEN
            r's `the representation is made`
        AND ((NOT r's `the representation is accurate`) OR det)
    -- 6. Representing that goods have been used to an extent different from the fact
    --    or that they have a particular history or use if the supplier knows it is
    --    not so.
    WHEN `Paragraph 6` r kn THEN
            `the representation is made and is untrue` r AND kn
    -- 7. Representing that goods or services are available ... if the supplier knows
    --    or can reasonably be expected to know it is not so, unless the
    --    representation clearly states any limitation.
    WHEN `Paragraph 7` r kn lim THEN
            `the representation is made and is untrue` r AND kn AND NOT lim
    -- 8. Representing that a service, part, repair or replacement is needed or
    --    desirable if that is not so, or that a service has been supplied ... if
    --    that is not so.
    WHEN `Paragraph 8` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 9. Representing that a price benefit or advantage exists ... where it does not.
    WHEN `Paragraph 9` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 10. Charging a price substantially higher than an estimate provided to the
    --     consumer, except where the consumer has expressly agreed to the higher
    --     price in advance.
    WHEN `Paragraph 10` est hi agreed THEN est AND hi AND NOT agreed
    -- 11. Representing that a transaction involves or does not involve rights,
    --     remedies or obligations where that representation is deceptive or
    --     misleading.
    WHEN `Paragraph 11` r dec THEN r's `the representation is made` AND dec
    -- 12. Representing that a person has or does not have the authority to negotiate
    --     the final terms of an agreement if the representation is different from
    --     the fact.
    WHEN `Paragraph 12` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 13. Taking advantage of a consumer by including in an agreement terms or
    --     conditions that are harsh, oppressive or excessively one-sided so as to be
    --     unconscionable.
    WHEN `Paragraph 13` inc harsh uncon THEN inc AND harsh AND uncon
    -- 14. Taking advantage of a consumer by exerting undue pressure or undue
    --     influence on the consumer to enter into a transaction.
    WHEN `Paragraph 14` pressure THEN pressure
    -- 15. Representing that another supplier will, on the presentment of a voucher,
    --     supply certain goods or services (or at a discount) when the supplier
    --     knows or ought to know they will not be.
    WHEN `Paragraph 15` rep kn THEN rep AND kn
    -- 16. Making a representation that appears in an objective form such as an
    --     editorial, documentary or scientific report when it is primarily made to
    --     sell goods or services, unless it states that it is an advertisement or a
    --     promotion.
    WHEN `Paragraph 16` obj sell adv THEN obj AND sell AND NOT adv
    -- 17. Representing that a particular person has offered or agreed to acquire
    --     goods or services whether or not at a stated price if the person has not.
    WHEN `Paragraph 17` rep did THEN rep AND NOT did
    -- 18. Representing the availability of facilities for repair of goods or of
    --     spare parts for goods if that is not the case.
    WHEN `Paragraph 18` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 19. Offering gifts, prizes or other free items in connection with the supply
    --     of goods or services if the supplier knows or ought to know that the items
    --     will not be provided or provided as offered.
    WHEN `Paragraph 19` offer kn THEN offer AND kn
    -- 20. Representing that goods or services are available at a discounted price for
    --     a stated period if the supplier knows or ought to know that they will
    --     continue to be so available for a substantially longer period.
    WHEN `Paragraph 20` rep kn THEN rep AND kn
    -- 21. Representing that goods or services are available at a discounted price
    --     for a particular reason that is different from the fact.
    WHEN `Paragraph 21` r THEN `the representation is made and is untrue` r
    -- 22. Making an invitation or offer at a certain price and then, with the
    --     intention of promoting different goods or services, (a) refusing to show or
    --     demonstrate, (b) refusing to take any order, (c) refusing to supply in a
    --     reasonable time, or (d) showing a defective sample.
    WHEN `Paragraph 22` inv intent ra rb rc rd THEN
            inv AND intent AND (ra OR rb OR rc OR rd)
    -- 23. Omitting to provide a material fact to a consumer, using small print to
    --     conceal a material fact or misleading a consumer as to a material fact, in
    --     connection with the supply of goods or services.
    WHEN `Paragraph 23` omit small mislead knows conn THEN
            (omit OR small OR mislead)
        AND `the information is a material fact` knows
        AND conn
    -- 24. Accepting payment or other consideration for the supply of goods or
    --     services when the supplier knows or ought to know that it will not be able
    --     to supply (a) within the period specified at or before the time of
    --     acceptance or (b) if none is specified, within a reasonable period.
    WHEN `Paragraph 24` accepts specified knowsperiod knowsreasonable THEN
            accepts
        AND (IF specified THEN knowsperiod ELSE knowsreasonable)
    -- 25. Purporting to assert a right to payment for the supply of unsolicited goods
    --     or services.
    WHEN `Paragraph 25` asserts unsol THEN asserts AND unsol
    -- 26. Sending to a consumer an invoice or document that states the amount of
    --     payment for unsolicited goods or services which does not contain, as its
    --     most prominent text, "This is not a bill. You are not required to pay any
    --     money.", unless the consumer has expressly acknowledged in writing the
    --     intention to accept and pay.
    WHEN `Paragraph 26` sends unsol prominent acked THEN
            sends AND unsol AND (NOT prominent) AND (NOT acked)
    -- 27. Where an applicable agreement has been entered into in writing and a copy
    --     has not been given, refusing to give the consumer a copy on request.
    WHEN `Paragraph 27` written nocopy requested refuses THEN
            written AND nocopy AND requested AND refuses
